  "review": {
    "review": "The initiating mistake was choosing a distant doorway while already standing on a usable open threshold. Decision 3528 (selection 10231) starts a seven-step exposed route toward door 335 instead of stepping off door 643 into observed cover. Decisions 3528–3533, accepted lines 10232–10252, show six retreat moves and health falling from 31 to zero. Two DM-100s were observed; one was initially sleeping. The evidence does not establish the final killer. An isolated original-source fixture reproduces the recorded first step, 598; this is not recovered runtime memory or a full-run reconstruction. The proposed narrow correction admits a clean, freshly visible adjacent bank behind the current door, screening every observed caster, and retains fresh arrival verification before waiting. It rejects hazards, loot-blocked closure and unscreened sleeping casters. The new regression fails as expected on original policy and passes on the candidate; all 2024 Python tests pass, with four skipped. This establishes a corrected selection, not survival or subsequent closure. The adapter will derive the changed policy and new test; files is intentionally empty.",
    "learnings": "Before crossing a lightning-exposed room toward another door, check whether stepping off the current threshold provides observed cover. Account for sleeping casters too, exclude heaps that prevent closure, and verify actual closure and exposure on arrival. A planned retreat is not proof of safety."
